 card." Sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step.)', 'Trample\\nWhenever Hoard Hauler deals combat damage to a player, create a Treasure token for each artifact they control.\\nCrew 3', "Trample\\nWhenever Ziatora's Envoy deals combat damage to a player, look at the top card of your library. You may play a land from the top of your library or cast a spell with mana value less than or equal to the damage dealt from the top of your library without paying its mana cost. If you don't, put that card into your hand.\\nBlitz {2}{B}{R}{G}", 'Tramway Station enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {R}.\\n{2}{B}{R}, {T}, Sacrifice Tramway Station: Draw a card.', 'Unleash the Inferno deals 7 damage to target creature or planeswalker. When it deals excess damage this way, destroy target artifact or enchantment an opponent controls with mana value less than or equal to that amount of excess damage.', 'Until end of turn, target artifact or creature becomes a 4/4 Angel artifact creature and gains flying.\\nDraw a card.', 'Until end of turn, target creature gets +2/+0 and gains "When this creature dies, return it to the battlefield tapped under its owner\'s control and you create a Treasure token." (It\'s an artifact with "{T}, Sacrifice this artifact: Add one mana of any color.")', 'Up to one target creature has base power and toughness 1/1 until end of turn. Up to one other target creature has base power and toughness 4/4 until end of turn. Then Hostile Takeover deals 3 damage to each creature.', 'Vigilance, trample\\nWhen Jewel Thief enters the battlefield, create a Treasure token. (It\'s an artifact with "{T}, Sacrifice this artifact: Add one mana of any color.")', 'Vigilance\\nMenace (This creature can\'t be blocked except by two or more creatures.)\\n{2}, Exile Masked Bandits from your hand: Target land gains "{T}: Add {B}, {R}, or {G}" until Masked Bandits is cast from exile. You may cast Masked Bandits for as long as it remains exiled.', 'Vigilance\\nWhen Brazen Upstart dies, look at the top five cards of your library. You may reveal a creature card from among them and put it into your hand. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.', "Vigilance\\nWhen Topiary Stomper enters the battlefield, search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.\\nTopiary Stomper can't attack or block unless you control seven or more lands.", 'Voice of the Vermin enters the battlefield with a shield counter on it. (If it would be dealt damage or destroyed, remove a shield counter from it instead.)\\nWhenever Voice of the Vermin attacks, target creature you control has base power and toughness 4/4 until end of turn.', 'Waterfront District enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {B}.\\n{2}{U}{B}, {T}, Sacrifice Waterfront District: Draw a card.', 'When Backup Agent enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.', 'When Brokers Hideout enters the battlefield, sacrifice it. When you do, search your library for a basic Forest, Plains, or Island card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle and you gain 1 life.', 'When Brokers Veteran dies, put a shield counter on target creature you control. (If it would be dealt damage or destroyed, remove a shield counter from it instead.)', 'When Cabaretti Courtyard enters the battlefield, sacrifice it. When you do, search your library for a basic Mountain, Forest, or Plains card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle and you gain 1 life.', 'When Caldaia Strongarm enters the battlefield, put two +1/+1 counters on target creature.\\nBlitz {3}{G} (If you cast this spell for its blitz cost, it gains haste and "When this creature dies, draw a card." Sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step.)', 'When Chrome Cat enters the battlefield, scry 1.', 'When Citizen\'s Crowbar enters the battlefield, create a 1/1 green and white Citizen creature token, then attach Citizen\'s Crowbar to it.\\nEquipped creature gets +1/+1 and has "{W}, {T}, Sacrifice Citizen\'s Crowbar: Destroy target artifact or enchantment."\\nEquip {2} ({2}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', 'When Cleanup Crew enters the battlefield, choose one —\\n• Destroy target artifact.\\n• Destroy target enchantment.\\n• Exile target card from a graveyard.\\n• You gain 4 life.', 'When Corpse Appraiser enters the battlefield, exile up to one target creature card from a graveyard. If a card is put into exile this way, look at the top three cards of your library, then put one of those cards into your hand and the rest into your graveyard.', 'When Corrupt Court Official enters the battlefield, target opponent discards a card.', "When Courier's Briefcase enters the battlefield, create a 1/1 green and white Citizen creature token.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Courier's Briefcase: Add one mana of any color.\\n{W}{U}{B}{R}{G}, {T}, Sacrifice Courier's Briefcase: Draw three cards.", 'When Exhibition Magician enters the battlefield, choose one —\\n• Create a 1/1 green and white Citizen creature token.\\n• Create a Treasure token. (It\'s an artifact with "{T}, Sacrifice this artifact: Add one mana of any color.")', 'When Gathering Throng enters the battlefield, you may search your library for any number of cards named Gathering Throng, reveal them, put them into your hand, then shuffle.', 'When Gilded Pinions enters the battlefield, create a Treasure token. (It\'s an artifact with "{T}, Sacrifice this artifact: Add one mana of any color.")\\nEquipped creature has flying.\\nEquip {2} ({2}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', 'When Girder Goons dies, create a tapped 2/2 black Rogue creature token.\\nBlitz {3}{B} (If you cast this spell for its blitz cost, it gains haste and "When this creature dies, draw a card." Sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step.)', 'When Glamorous Outlaw enters the battlefield, it deals 2 damage to each opponent and you scry 2.\\n{2}, Exile Glamorous Outlaw from your hand: Target land gains "{T}: Add {U}, {B}, or {R}" until Glamorous Outlaw is cast from exile. You may cast Glamorous Outlaw for as long as it remains exiled.', 'When Lagrella, the Magpie enters the battlefield, exile any number of other target creatures controlled by different players until Lagrella leaves the battlefield. When an exiled card enters the battlefield under your control this way, put two +1/+1 counters on it.', 'When Lord Xander, the Collector enters the battlefield, target opponent discards half the cards in their hand, rounded down.\\nWhenever Lord Xander attacks, defending player mills half their library, rounded down.\\nWhen Lord Xander dies, target opponent sacrifices half the nonland permanents they control, rounded down.', 'When Maestros Theater enters the battlefield, sacrifice it. When you do, search your library for a basic Island, Swamp, or Mountain card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle and you gain 1 life.', 'When Mage\'s Attendant enters the battlefield, create a 1/1 blue Wizard creature token with "{1}, Sacrifice this creature: Counter target noncreature spell unless its controller pays {1}."', 'When Night Clubber enters the battlefield, creatures your opponents control get -1/-1 until end of turn.\\nBlitz {2}{B} (If you cast this spell for its blitz cost, it gains haste and "When this creature dies, draw a card." Sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step.)', 'When Obscura Storefront enters the battlefield, sacrifice it. When you do, search your library for a basic Plains, Island, or Swamp card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle and you gain 1 life.', "When Psychic Pickpocket enters the battlefield, it connives. When it connives this way, return up to one target nonland permanent to its owner's hand. (To have a creature connive, draw a card, then discard a card. If you discarded a nonland card, put a +1/+1 counter on that creature.)", "When Raffine's Informant enters the battlefield, it connives. (Draw a card, then discard a card. If you discarded a nonland card, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature.)", "When Raffine's Silencer enters the battlefield, it connives. (Draw a card, then discard a card. If you discarded a nonland card, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature.)\\nWhen Raffine's Silencer dies, target creature an opponent controls gets -X/-X until end of turn, where X is Raffine's Silencer's power.", 'When Rakish Revelers enters the battlefield, create a 1/1 green and white Citizen creature token.\\n{2}, Exile Rakish Revelers from your hand: Target land gains "{T}: Add {R}, {G}, or {W}" until Rakish Revelers is cast from exile. You may cast Rakish Revelers for as long as it remains exiled.', 'When Riveteers Overlook enters the battlefield, sacrifice it. When you do, search your library for a basic Swamp, Mountain, or Forest card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle and you gain 1 life.', 'When Riveteers Requisitioner dies, create a Treasure token. (It\'s an artifact with "{T}, Sacrifice this artifact: Add one mana of any color.")\\nBlitz {2}{R} (If you cast this spell for its blitz cost, it gains haste and "When this creature dies, draw a card." Sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step.)', 'When Rocco, Cabaretti Caterer enters the battlefield, if you cast it, you may search your library for a creature card with mana value X or less, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'When Snooping Newsie enters the battlefield, mill two cards. (Put the top two cards of your library into your graveyard.)\\nAs long as there are five or more mana values among cards in your graveyard, Snooping Newsie gets +1/+1 and has lifelink.', 'When Soul of Emancipation enters the battlefield, destroy up to three other target nonland permanents. For each of those permanents, its controller creates a 3/3 white Angel creature token with flying.', 'When Spara\'s Adjudicators enters the battlefield, target creature an opponent controls can\'t attack or block until your next turn.\\n{2}, Exile Spara\'s Adjudicators from your hand: Target land gains "{T}: Add {G}, {W}, or {U}" until Spara\'s Adjudicators is cast from exile. You may cast Spara\'s Adjudicators for as long as it remains exiled.', 'When Stimulus Package enters the battlefield, create two Treasure tokens. (They\'re artifacts with "{T}, Sacrifice this artifact: Add one mana of any color.")\\nSacrifice a Treasure: Create a 1/1 green and white Citizen creature token.', "When Toluz, Clever Conductor enters the battlefield, it connives. (Draw a card, then discard a card. If you discarded a nonland card, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature.)\\nWhenever you discard one or more cards, exile them from your graveyard.\\nWhen Toluz dies, put the cards exiled with it into their owner's hand.", 'When Unlucky Witness dies, exile the top two cards of your library. Until your next end step, you may play one of those cards.', 'When you cast this spell, copy it. (The copy becomes a token.)\\nEquipped creature has double strike as long as two or more Equipment are attached to it.\\nEquip {1} ({1}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', 'Whenever Ballroom Brawlers attacks, Ballroom Brawlers and up to one other target creature you control both gain your choice of first strike or lifelink until end of turn.', 'Whenever Civic Gardener attacks, untap target creature or land.', 'Whenever Civil Servant attacks, you may tap another untapped Citizen you control. If you do, Civil Servant gets +1/+0 and gains lifelink until end of turn.', 'Whenever Freelance Muscle attacks or blocks, it gets +X/+X until end of turn, where X is the greatest power and/or toughness among other creatures you control.', "Whenever Mysterious Limousine enters the battlefield or attacks, exile up to one other target creature until Mysterious Limousine leaves the battlefield. If a creature is put into exile this way, return each other card exiled with Mysterious Limousine to the battlefield under its owner's control.\\nCrew 2", 'Whenever Plasma Jockey attacks, target creature an opponent controls can\'t block this turn.\\nBlitz {2}{R} (If you cast this spell for its blitz cost, it gains haste and "When this creature dies, draw a card." Sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step.)', 'Whenever Pugnacious Pugilist attacks, create a tapped and attacking 1/1 red Devil creature token with "When this creature dies, it deals 1 damage to any target."\\nBlitz {3}{R} (If you cast this spell for its blitz cost, it gains haste and "When this creature dies, draw a card." Sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step.)', "Whenever you attack, double target creature's power until end of turn.", 'Whenever you cast a spell, if its mana value is equal to 1 plus the number of soul counters on Obscura Ascendancy, put a soul counter on Obscura Ascendancy, then create a 2/2 white Spirit creature token with flying.\\nAs long as there are five or more soul counters on Obscura Ascendancy, Spirits you control get +3/+3.', 'Whenever you cast your first instant or sorcery spell each turn, exile an instant or sorcery card at random from your graveyard. Then copy each card exiled with Arcane Bombardment. You may cast any number of the copies without paying their mana costs.', 'Whenever you draw a card, target opponent loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever you sacrifice a creature, you may return target creature card with lesser mana value from your graveyard to the battlefield tapped. Do this only once each turn.', "Whenever you sacrifice another creature, put a +1/+1 counter on Body Dropper.\\n{B}{R}, Sacrifice another creature: Body Dropper gains menace until end of turn. (It can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.)", 'Whenever you sacrifice one or more other creatures, Forge Boss deals 2 damage to each opponent. This ability triggers only once each turn.', 'Wingshield Agent enters the battlefield with a shield counter on it. (If it would be dealt damage or destroyed, remove a shield counter from it instead.)\\nWhenever Wingshield Agent attacks, up to one other target creature gains flying until end of turn.', 'You may have Undercover Operative enter the battlefield as a copy of any creature on the battlefield, except it enters with a shield counter on it if you control that creature. (If it would be dealt damage or destroyed, remove a shield counter from it instead.)', "You may pay {R}{G} rather than pay this spell's mana cost. Spend only mana produced by Treasures to cast it this way.", '[+1]: Choose up to one target creature. Put a +1/+1 counter and a counter from among flying, first strike, lifelink, or vigilance on it.\\n[−3]: Look at the top seven cards of your library. You may put a permanent card with mana value 3 or less from among them onto the battlefield with a shield counter on it. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.\\n[−7]: Create five 3/3 white Angel creature tokens with flying.', "[+2]: You may sacrifice a creature. If you do, search your library for a creature card with mana value equal to 1 plus the sacrificed creature's mana value, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.\\n[+1]: Mill five cards, then put any number of creature cards milled this way into your hand.\\n[−1]: Create a 4/4 green Rhino Warrior creature token.", "{1}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature: Count the colors of the sacrificed creature, then search your library for a creature card that's exactly that many colors plus one. Exile that card, then shuffle. You may cast the exiled card. Activate only as a sorcery.", "{1}, {T}: Pyre-Sledge Arsonist deals X damage to any target, where X is the number of permanents you've sacrificed this turn.", '{1}{B/G}: Riveteers Initiate gains deathtouch until end of turn.', '{1}{U}, Exile Expendable Lackey from your graveyard: Create a 1/1 blue Fish creature token with "This creature can\'t be blocked." Activate only as a sorcery.', '{2}, Exile Halo Scarab from your graveyard: Create a Treasure token. (It\'s an artifact with "{T}, Sacrifice this artifact: Add one mana of any color.")', '{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Ominous Parcel: Search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.\\n{5}, {T}, Sacrifice Ominous Parcel: It deals 4 damage to target creature.', '{2}{R/W}: Cabaretti Initiate gains double strike until end of turn.', '{3}: Hypnotic Grifter connives. (Draw a card, then discard a card. If you discarded a nonland card, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature.)', "{3}{U}: Sewer Crocodile can't be blocked this turn. This ability costs {3} less to activate if there are five or more mana values among cards in your graveyard.", '{4}{G/U}: Brokers Initiate has base power and toughness 5/5 until end of turn.', '{4}{U/R}, Exile Maestros Initiate from your graveyard: Draw two cards, then discard a card.', '{R}, {T}, Discard a card: Create a token that\'s a copy of another target creature you control. It gains haste and "When this creature dies, draw a card." Sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step. Activate only as a sorcery.\\nBlitz {1}{R} (If you cast this spell for its blitz cost, it gains haste and "When this creature dies, draw a card." Sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step.)', "{R}{G}: Jetmir's Fixer gets +1/+1 until end of turn. If mana from a Treasure was spent to activate this ability, put a +1/+1 counter on Jetmir's Fixer instead.", '{T}, Pay 3 life: Flip a coin. If you win the flip, you gain 6 life.', '{T}: Add {R}. Put a stash counter on Glittering Stockpile.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Glittering Stockpile: Add X mana of any one color, where X is the number of stash counters on Glittering Stockpile.', '{T}: Create a Treasure token. (It\'s an artifact with "{T}, Sacrifice this artifact: Add one mana of any color.")', "{T}: Exile up to two target cards from a single graveyard.\\nUnlicensed Hearse's power and toughness are each equal to the number of cards exiled with it.\\nCrew 2", '{W}, {T}, Untap a tapped creature you control: Create a 1/1 green and white Citizen creature token.\\n{W}{W}, {T}, Untap two tapped creatures you control: Draw a card.\\n{W}{W}{W}{W}{W}, {T}, Untap fifteen tapped creatures you control: You win the game.']
flavor: ['"All is calm. All is well. You know me to be a trusted member of your family, and I would like to discuss the contents of our safe."', '"Altonio? No, I\'m sorry. No one by that name works here."\\n—Raffine', '"Angels are living proof that power does not always lead to corruption."\\n—Elspeth', '"Big furnace like this can reduce anything to ash. You got something you need reduced to ash?"', '"Breaking news! Lord Xander found dead! Suspect at large!"', '"Build your towers as tall as you want. The shadow always reaches higher."\\n—Message scrawled on an alley wall', '"Crisp, flavorful, and energizing. Perhaps the most elegant offering of Halo in Park Heights. Five stars."\\n—Conzuelo, restaurant critic', '"Don\'t tell me who sent you or who you work for. The less I know, the better."', '"Feed the rumor mills with delicious treachery. Bad blood between those two is a good deal for us."\\n—Kamiz, Obscura Oculus', '"Fried squid, comin\' up!"', '"Greedy vault guard, wouldn\'t share. Now there\'s Halo in your hair!"', '"How far are you willing to go for your family, cleanblade?"\\n—Lord Xander', '"I always say, \'If it\'s breathing, it\'s lying.\' Luckily my friend here does neither."\\n—Lord Xander', '"I could show you what\'s in the case, but it\'d be the last thing you ever see."', '"I have exactly what you need. The question is, how badly do you need it?"', '"I was never here."', '"I wouldn\'t call what they have here a justice system. More like an auction."\\n—Elspeth', '"I\'m fresh out of mercy today. Why don\'t you ask Sparky here for forgiveness?"', '"I\'ve analyzed the vault schematic. Do you want the fast way, the easy way, or the secret way in?"', '"I\'ve known for a year that you would cast this exact spell, at this exact spot, at this exact time."\\n—Raffine', '"I\'ve told you knuckleheads a hundred times: You can kill \'em here, but bury the bodies somewhere else. If you disturb my prized azaleas again, you\'d better dig a second hole for yourself!"', '"If I were you, I\'d check that elf\'s coat. I saw him slipping something into his pocket just before you arrived."\\n—Krandal, freelance instigator', '"If you wish for blessings, mortal, ask your demon masters. We\'ve given enough to your kind."', '"In the assassination trade, no one lives to make more than one mistake."\\n—Anhelo, the Painter', '"It\'s all about who you know, darling. And now you\'re lucky enough to know me."', '"It\'s delightful, the things their owners reveal when they think no one is listening."', '"It\'s just business. You understand."', '"It\'s too quiet tonight. Go make trouble."\\n—Ziatora', '"Kill count? I lost track years ago."', '"Let\'s find out how much your friends think you\'re worth."\\n—Gino, hired kidnapper', '"Look, we both get what we want. I get your Halo. You get to keep your kneecaps."', '"My sources say the Beamtown Bullies were spotted in the Mezzio. Keep your eyes sharp and stay close to me."', '"Nothing to see here. Just carrying a carpet. Yes, the carpet wears boots. Stop asking questions."', '"Now there\'s a fellow who knows how to have a good time!"\\n—Jetmir', '"Only a chump stops after one unlucky loss. You\'re not a chump, are you?"', '"Quick, let\'s hide in the sewer!"\\n—Ginsi the Thief, now deceased', '"Saving a stranger\'s life is an excellent recruitment method. Luckily, peril is so easy to come by."\\n—Falco Spara', '"Say hello to my little friend."', '"Scarcely a mark. A true work of art!"', '"Subsequent efforts to deconstruct this facility will be punished with increasing severity."', '"Subtlety is overrated."\\n—Mr. Orfeo, the Boulder', '"Terribly sorry, but this is a private party, and your name isn\'t on the list."', '"The little guy had guts at least. You can see \'em right there between those cobbles."\\n—Glunk, freelance crusher', '"They can afford the loss. They build it into their prices."', '"This city could certainly use a bit more divine intervention."\\n—Inspector Jillard', '"This is the beginning of a beautiful friendship. And more importantly, a profitable one. Now sign here."', '"Together we can build a safer, brighter New Capenna!"', '"Trust me, you want to deal with me. My associates are much less pleasant."', '"Unimaginable riches? I assure you, I have a *vivid* imagination."', '"Up and at \'em, buddy. We\'ve got more work to do."', '"We are this city, down to its bones."', '"We\'re family now, big guy."', '"Welcome to the family. Chef Rocco sends their congratulations."', '"Well, I guess stealth\'s out of the question."', '"Well, that\'s one way to scatter her ashes."\\n—Calvey, funeral director', '"Whatever ails you, friends, this will cure it for tonight! And leave you with a little inspiration for tomorrow."', '"Whatever you\'re looking for—food, family, Halo—we\'ve got the best in town."', '"Where did I find my horned friend? Now there\'s a story worth telling. . . ."', '"You bore me."', 'A plus-one is simply not enough.', 'A ten-minute ride can take you to the luxury of Park Heights, or the grit of the Caldaia.', 'After a brief but memorable incident at her first performance, she was never heckled again.', 'After diverting around the eleventh construction barrier, the taxi driver began to suspect she was being herded into a trap.', 'After the attack on the Vantoleone, the fragile balance of power shattered completely, and the city descended into chaos.', 'Along the outer girders, in gold filigree, are inscribed the names of all those who fell to their deaths during construction.', 'As Ob Nixilis closed in, Halo swept through Giada like an electrical current, and inside her, something long dormant unfurled its wings.', 'As the Adversary\'s forces descended upon the gala, Elspeth whispered to Giada, "I can get you out of here, but we have to go now."', 'As the assassins converged on Kitt Kanto, she struck a high note and held it, unbroken, for nearly a minute. When the room fell silent, she was surrounded only by rose petals falling gently to the floor.', 'Better to depart in haste than be dearly departed.', "Between the five of them, they'd committed every crime on the books and invented a few new ones.", 'Bits of the missing agent were discovered in various alleys across all three boroughs.', 'Brokers agents defend their charges by all means available, from intricate logic to blunt force trauma.', 'Construction in New Capenna is imbued with tradition and ritual.', 'Crime sometimes makes unlikely allies into lifelong friends.', "Descended from Old Capenna's paladins, the Brokers are masters of defensive combat.", "Don't try to cut in. They'll cut back.", 'Elspeth wanted answers. Xander needed a spy. Their paths were destined to cross.', "Every Halo smuggler walks a razor's edge between untold riches and sudden disaster.", 'Everybody is worth their weight in gold.', "Everything from damaged furniture to inconvenient corpses becomes fuel for Ziatora's ever-burning foundry.", 'Few know her face, but everyone knows her work.', 'For the next week, Park Heights smelled of burnt oil paint and brimstone.', 'For those who need to make a quick departure without attracting undue attention.', 'For years, the five families ruled New Capenna in uneasy peace, and the city prospered.', 'He keeps the heat off his allies—by drawing it all to himself.', 'He never asks why. Just who, when, and where.', 'Her opponent threw her through the window, so she retaliated by throwing the window through her opponent.', "If you're lucky, you'll walk out with just your ego singed.", 'In volatile times, a sense of certainty is in high demand.', 'In with the old, out with the new.', "Investigators observed that Altonio's beloved fish were thriving after his disappearance.", "It pulses with the colors that best complement the wearer's outfit.", 'Labyrinths of tunnels beneath the streets of the Caldaia offer an ample array of discreet routes for enterprising smugglers.', 'Light poured from every crack as the sleepers awoke from their long stone slumber.', 'Maestros agents can lie low in high style at the opulent Shadow Hostel.', 'Mikey "the Mouth" kept his nickname after he struck his deal with Gregorio, even though he never spoke another word.', "New Capenna's demonic masters are quick to extinguish any hint of the angels' power reawakening.", "New Capenna's districts are a series of tiers; wealth and power always rise to the top.", "New Capenna's statues hold Old Capenna's secrets.", 'No evidence, no crime.', 'No institution, however grand, can withstand the collective will of the people.', 'No one remains on her list for long.', 'No screams rang out. No blood stained the streets. In an instant, the bustling metropolis simply fell silent.', 'No true angels have been created since the founding of New Capenna, but artisans have learned to craft elegant facsimiles.', 'Nobody thought twice about checking their weapons at the door, until they were informed there was no weapon check at the door.', "Ob Nixilis decided the fastest way to seize control of New Capenna would be to usurp the networks of power already hidden there. Xander's Maestros were the first to fall.", 'Ob Nixilis extends his hand not in partnership, but to affirm your subservience.', 'Ob Nixilis smiled. It had been over one thousand years since his last conquest.', 'Obscura initiates are required to bring a gift of information. They are judged on both how useful it is and how hard it was to obtain.', 'Once he was jumped by a dozen Maestros agents. You can still see their imprints in the pavement if you know where to look.', 'Once the witness was inside, the safe house vanished first from sight, then from memory.', 'One last job before he retires.', 'Only extraordinary performers are invited to grace the grandest stage in New Capenna.', 'Overnight, Elspeth was branded the most dangerous criminal in New Capenna.', 'Porter, cleaner, and bouncer all in one.', 'Public parks are a favored meeting spot for those considering a shift in allegiance.', 'Purchasing chrome racehorses with cash is a common means of dispersing mysterious income.', 'Regarding the relative might of pen and sword, the official position of the Brokers is "Why choose?"', 'Restless Riveteers can always find a sparring partner in the sprawling Treza warehouse.', 'She knows your next move before you do.', 'She sees the world as a gift meant for her.', "She watches Jetmir's back while her companions watch hers.", 'Slicing girders, rescuing trapped workers, killing gigantic rust flies—one tool does it all!', 'So long as the Halo keeps flowing, the festivities never end.', 'Some try to unravel the tangled skeins of fate. She reweaves them to her own deadly design.', "Steel doors and iron bars are child's play for an Obscura operative.", 'Still and solemn as the statues of her kind that decorated the Park Heights rooftops, she gazed in sorrow on the city below.', 'Street corners in the Mezzio are a tantalizing bazaar of the fantastic, the illicit, and the fake.', 'The Cabaretti cultivate an image of harmless hedonism, happy for the other families to underestimate their formidable firepower.', 'The Obscura reserve their keenest blades for traitors in their midst.', "The Obscura's Cloud Spire dominates the skyline, its eye a beacon of progress that sees all.", 'The Riveteers are as good at raising buildings as they are at razing them.', 'The Vanto Beatdown began as an improvised dance-battle at the Rose Room lounge. When word spread of how many were slain at the first event, it became a citywide obsession.', 'The bottom of the dark canals is littered with countless corpses and treasures.', 'The broad avenues and graceful spires of Park Heights are the playground of the affluent. After nightfall, they also make a fine hunting ground.', 'The burglar turned, bowed, and dropped from the ledge onto her waiting mount.', 'The fights may sometimes be rigged, but the front-row spectators know the wounds are real.', 'The great library in the Museum of Old Capenna has a million volumes on display—and miles of passages hidden behind them.', 'The guard took a midnight shift to earn a promotion. Unfortunately, so did the assassin.', "The mansion's vaulted ceilings provided the perfect cover for an ambush.", 'The only thing Ziatora desires is "more."', 'The parklike Cabaretti grounds offer rest, food, and the perfect place to shake off a tail.', 'The people flocked to the glittering parade, turning their backs on the threats in the shadows.', 'The rendezvous took place hours ago, but the Obscura agent read the residue with ease.', "The rest of Anhelo's assistant arrived over the following week.", "The source of the Cabaretti's Halo turned out to be a single teenage girl.", 'The staccato clatter of its metal claws on pavement is unmistakable.', 'Their toast to good health went immediately, horribly awry.', "They built the neighborhood. They know its weak points. They know all the hiding places. When they come for you, they'll find you and bring the roof down on your head.", "They wouldn't admit it, but some people join the Cabaretti just for the food.", "They'd warned him greed would be the death of him. He never thought to take it literally.", 'Those who try to rob the Obscura often leave behind more than they take away.', "To most, the Nido Sanctuary is an office complex. To the Brokers, it's a vault of secrets.", 'Underweight, underpaid, underestimated.', 'Unlucky assassins find out why he\'s called "Brick Wall" Balzano.', "Whatever the Maestros had ordered, it wasn't anyone's business, including his.", 'When all you have is a warhammer, every face looks like a nail.', "When you lose Jetmir's trust, his family makes sure you lose everything else.", "Young viashino flock to the Riveteers for Ziatora's leadership, eager to unleash their own inner dragons.", "Ziatora's second-in-command has a habit of appearing when and where her enemies least expect her."]
